## 7. PHASE 2 — PROBLEM DEFINITION

### Current State

```text
- tightly coupled FE and BE
- auth logic in frontend
- session stored in file
- no separation of concerns
```

---

### Expected State

```text
- FE independent from BE
- BE handles auth and logic
- session centralized (Redis)
- API-first architecture
```

---

### Core Problem

```text
System is not designed for distributed architecture and cannot scale safely.
```

---

## 8. PHASE 3 — TARGET ARCHITECTURE DESIGN

### Architecture

```text
FE (Next.js) → API → BE (Laravel) → DB
                       ↓
                    Redis
                       ↓
                  Keycloak
```

---

### Responsibility Split

| Layer    | Responsibility        |
| -------- | --------------------- |
| FE       | UI only               |
| BE       | auth + business logic |
| Keycloak | identity              |
| DB       | authorization         |
| Redis    | session               |

---

## 9. PHASE 4 — KEYCLOAK ENGINEERING

### Objective

```text
Use Keycloak as identity provider only
```

---

### Required Configuration

```text
Realm: client-portal
Client: client-portal-fe

✔ Standard flow enabled
✔ PKCE (S256) enabled
✔ Confidential client
✔ Valid redirect URIs updated (production domain)
```

---

### Critical Rules

```text
❌ do not trust Keycloak roles
✔ only trust DB roles
✔ BE performs token exchange
✔ FE never sees tokens
```

---

### Security Hardening

```text
✔ replace temporary admin user
✔ enforce strong credentials
✔ restrict redirect URIs
✔ disable unused flows
```

---

## 10. PHASE 5 — BACKEND DEVELOPMENT (FROM ZERO)

### Objective

```text
Build Laravel backend as system authority
```

---

### Core Modules

```text
Auth Controller
Session Service (Redis)
User Mapping Service
RBAC Module
Project/Task Domain Services
Audit Logger
```

---

### Auth Flow

```text
GET /auth/login
→ redirect to Keycloak

GET /auth/callback
→ exchange code
→ create session

GET /auth/me
→ return current user

POST /auth/logout
→ destroy session
```

---

### Session Implementation

```text
Storage: Redis

✔ create
✔ read
✔ refresh
✔ expire
✔ destroy
```

---

### Enforcement

```text
✔ middleware for session validation
✔ role enforcement
✔ ownership enforcement
```

---

## 11. PHASE 6 — FRONTEND REFACTOR

### Objective

```text
Transform FE into pure presentation layer
```

---

### Remove

```text
❌ internal API routes
❌ session logic
❌ auth handling
❌ business logic
```

---

### Add

```text
✔ API client (fetch/axios)
✔ auth-aware routing
✔ error handling UI
✔ loading states
```

---

### Pattern

```text
FE → call BE API
BE → returns JSON
FE → render UI
```

---

## 12. PHASE 7 — API CONTRACT

### Structure

```text
/api/v1/*
```

---

### Segmentation

```text
